    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Counting to ten",
     "texto": [
      "The numbers from cero to diez are: **cero, uno, dos, tres, cuatro, cinco, seis, siete, ocho, nueve, diez**.\n\nTo say your age you use **tener**, not **ser**:\n\n- **Tengo siete años.** (correct)\n- *Soy siete años.* (incorrect)\n\nTo ask: **¿Cuántos años tienes?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Years are had",
     "texto": [
      "In Spanish, age is given with the verb **tener**:\n\n- yo **tengo**\n- tú **tienes**\n- él / ella / usted **tiene**\n\n**Tengo diez años** means «I have ten years of life». Saying «soy diez años» is a very common mistake: it sounds as if you were a number."
     ],
